NAME
    ps, jobs - list active breakpoints, watches, and sessions

SYNOPSIS
    ps
    jobs

DESCRIPTION
    Lists every active breakpoint (see 'bp'), watch (see 'watch'), and tmux
    session (see 'tmux', if a session manager is registered for this host)
    as one unified table - the read-only counterpart to 'kill'. 'jobs' is a
    plain alias, not a separate command. Each row's id column is exactly
    what 'kill' expects: 'bp<N>' for a breakpoint, 'watch<N>' for a watch, or
    a session's own name - copy a row's id straight into 'kill' unchanged.
    Prints nothing wrong, just an empty-looking table, with no ROM loaded and
    no session manager registered (there's nothing to list, not an error).

EXAMPLES
    ps
    jobs
